__label__books let me hear your voice a family's triumph over autism from the inside flap autiful doelike child with an intense graceful fragility in her first year she picked up words smiled and laughed and learned to walk but then anne marie began to turn inward and when her little girl lost some of the words she had acquired cried inconsolably and showed no interest in anyone around her catherine maurice took her to doctors who gave her a devastating diagnosis autism in their desperate struggle to save their daughter the maurices plunged into a medical nightmare of false hopes miracle cures and infuriating suggestions that anne marie's autism was somehow their fault finally anne marie was saved by an intensive behavioral therapy let me hear your voice is a mother's illuminating account of how one family triumphed over autism it is an absolutely unforgettable book as beautifully written as it is informative a vivid and uplifting story offers new strength to parents who refuse to give up on their autistic children k 				 	 					 about the author catherine maurice is a pseudonym
